rem Subsets with a Unique Sum
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=201
rem Add the sums reached by exactly one
rem K-element subset of the first Count
rem squares

use bits
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Count integer = 100
option K integer = 50

rem One[k] and Many[k] are bit sets of
rem the sums reached by one, or by more
rem than one, k-subset. Each square
rem shifts both sets up one size.
One = array shape (K + 1) fill 0
One 0 = 1
Many = One - One
Z = array 0
for Q in 1 to Count
  Sq = Q * Q
  S1 = (concat Z (One take K)) Sq shl
  SM = (concat Z (Many take K)) Sq shl
  Both = One S1 band
  Many = Many SM bor Both bor
  One = (One S1 bor) (Many bnot) band
end
Top = One K
Cap = (1 to Count array) ** 2 sum
Sums = 0 to Cap array
Hit' = Top Sums bit
Used' = Sums filter Hit
Answer = Used sum
Answer print
